WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.750
It's midday in London.

2
00:00:01.800 --> 00:00:03.970
You video-call a friend in China.

3
00:00:04.020 --> 00:00:06.230
For them, it's already evening.

4
00:00:06.280 --> 00:00:09.170
Then you call a cousin in
the eastern United States.

5
00:00:09.220 --> 00:00:11.250
There, it's still morning.

6
00:00:11.300 --> 00:00:14.750
So why isn't it midday
everywhere at the same time?

7
00:00:14.800 --> 00:00:18.470
In this mission, you'll learn
lines of latitude and longitude,

8
00:00:18.520 --> 00:00:20.780
and the two lines marked zero degrees.

9
00:00:20.830 --> 00:00:23.010
You'll split the Earth
into hemispheres,

10
00:00:23.060 --> 00:00:25.890
and name the special
circles on the map.

11
00:00:25.940 --> 00:00:27.910
Then you'll see how time zones work.

12
00:00:27.960 --> 00:00:32.190
Your mission: explain why the
clock changes as you travel

13
00:00:32.240 --> 00:00:33.610
around the world.
